WEBVTT

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.730
It's all hot and muggy...

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:08.970
The humidity...

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.740
Bad job.

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:14.720
Japan's rainy season is the worst!

00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:18.180
And on top of that, this school 
has no air conditioning...

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:20.110
I can't understand it!

00:00:21.070 --> 00:00:22.630
The liquid resin...

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:24.870
isn't drying very well.

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:31.250
Meow...

00:00:30.100 --> 00:00:32.420
Everyone, listen for a moment, if you will.

00:00:32.990 --> 00:00:36.570
Making small items to 
fund our secret hideout plan...

00:00:37.040 --> 00:00:40.540
is difficult with this heat and humidity,

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:44.490
so, during the rainy season, what do 
you think about working at my house?

00:00:44.490 --> 00:00:46.140
At your house, Leadercchi?

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:47.630
Well...

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:50.400
The other day, you said you'd 
come over to hang out, right?

00:00:50.830 --> 00:00:52.730
So I thought, um...

00:00:52.730 --> 00:00:54.710
Yes! I'll go!

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:55.640
Y-Yes!

00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:57.060
Of course!

00:00:57.660 --> 00:01:00.330
Then, that's that.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:04.340
You do have air conditioning, don't you?

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:38.010
This is delicious!

00:02:38.010 --> 00:02:43.390
<b>Step 7
"DIY" Means You Can Do Things Inside If It's Hot and Muggy Out</b>

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:41.460
The okonomiyaki has cabbage and pork,

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:44.610
and the ramen has lots 
of pork back fat in it.

00:02:45.110 --> 00:02:48.480
But if you're going to visit 
your club leader's house,

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:50.340
you'll need some kind of 
gift to take with you.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:52.350
It's something we were given as a gift,

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:55.250
but we have some senbei 
crackers. Take those.

00:02:56.050 --> 00:02:58.100
Thank you, mother.

00:02:58.110 --> 00:03:00.610
<b>Sukonbu 
Snack</b>

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:03.220
Hot chocolate and sukonbu?

00:03:03.790 --> 00:03:06.110
What does that combination 
taste like together?

00:03:06.110 --> 00:03:09.870
Hot chocolate is best with sukonbu.

00:03:10.180 --> 00:03:11.280
Really?

00:03:11.280 --> 00:03:12.290
Sure!

00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:14.800
If you're going to visit 
your club leader's house,

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:17.110
why don't you take the
 baumkuchen with you?

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.260
It was something someone
 gave to me, though.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.060
Why?

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.290
How do you say it in English? 
A souvenir? A gift?

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:28.420
You say, "I know it isn't much, 
but..." and give it to them.

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:30.050
Okay, Pudding.

00:03:30.270 --> 00:03:33.820
Japanese thoughtfulness. Good job!

00:03:39.270 --> 00:03:41.310
Wow!

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:45.340
This one! And that one! All of them! 
Screws! Screws! Screws!

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.320
Wood Screws

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:43.320
Partially Threaded 
Wood Screws

00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:45.320
Micro Screws

00:03:45.340 --> 00:03:50.340
It's just one word, "screw," but 
there are so many different kinds!

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:52.480
14.4 volts.

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:54.450
Seems like it'd have a good amount of power.

00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:56.410
This hammer is so big!

00:03:56.410 --> 00:03:58.450
I wonder what it's used for, meow!

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.220
WAKUWAN Workshop

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.220
Self-service

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.220
Workspace

00:03:58.460 --> 00:04:01.220
Even without tools,
even without experience
feel free to Try DIY!

00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:01.220
Everyone, come over here please!

00:04:12.150 --> 00:04:14.520
Wow!

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.180
Quite the skills.

00:04:17.180 --> 00:04:19.440
Why are you talking like you're 
the superior one here?

00:04:20.690 --> 00:04:21.780
Welcome.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.560
You're the DIY club, right?

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:28.610
Waku Wan's managing director, my dad.

00:04:28.610 --> 00:04:30.280
Thank you for having us!

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:32.960
Rei told me about your project.

00:04:33.260 --> 00:04:35.970
You're free to use anything 
that's over there.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.960
What? All of it?

00:04:38.960 --> 00:04:42.160
Well, we can't sell any of it anyway.

00:04:42.160 --> 00:04:44.460
Do your best building your secret hideout.

00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:46.420
Thank you, we will!

00:04:51.990 --> 00:04:53.130
Do you think you can use it?

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:56.970
Wow. This board is so smooth! 
It feels really nice!

00:04:57.460 --> 00:04:59.540
There are all kinds of things here.

00:05:02.850 --> 00:05:04.530
These aprons...

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:08.270
These screws are rusty, but they're 
still totally usable, meow!

00:05:08.270 --> 00:05:13.040
Do we have to carry all this 
stuff back to the school?

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:14.760
Where's the manager?

00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:16.470
Your mama's out on a delivery.

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:17.280
This is awesome, meow!

00:05:16.470 --> 00:05:17.710
Oh.

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:18.540
Right?

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:21.800
Director, there's a call from a customer!

00:05:18.850 --> 00:05:20.200
Yeah!

00:05:21.350 --> 00:05:24.980
This one, too, meow.

00:05:21.800 --> 00:05:23.060
All right!

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:24.550
Well, take your time.

00:05:25.610 --> 00:05:28.970
For now, how about we go to my room?

00:05:36.740 --> 00:05:39.230
It's so cute!

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.660
Meow!

00:05:40.800 --> 00:05:42.420
It's lovely!

00:05:42.420 --> 00:05:44.730
Is it? Thanks.

00:05:45.010 --> 00:05:48.870
For the leader of the DIY club, 
this much is only to be expected.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.480
Really, why are you talking like 
you're the superior one here?

00:05:51.750 --> 00:05:54.150
Did you make this, too, Leadercchi?

00:05:54.150 --> 00:05:54.990
Yeah.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.240
And this...

00:05:56.430 --> 00:05:57.490
and this?

00:05:57.670 --> 00:05:58.990
And this, too?

00:05:59.180 --> 00:06:03.010
That coffee dripper is a favorite of mine, 
even though I made it myself.

00:06:03.010 --> 00:06:06.630
Wow! This is really nice, meow!
 I really like it, meow!

00:06:06.630 --> 00:06:08.420
You drink coffee?

00:06:08.420 --> 00:06:12.760
We use butter-roasted coffee beans
at home, and I drink it all the time.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:15.530
I've heard of butter coffee.

00:06:15.530 --> 00:06:18.310
That's a different thing though.

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:19.530
Oh!

00:06:20.770 --> 00:06:24.760
This is the bookshelf 
that I put the screw in!

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:28.640
It was the first time
 I'd used an electric driver,

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:32.640
so there was a bit of a commotion 
and the screw ended up crooked.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.450
<i>Sunflower Girls</i>

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.450
<i>Sunflower Girls</i>

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:38.390
But our club leader was nice 
enough to use it anyway!

00:06:39.250 --> 00:06:40.830
C-Club leader!

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.340
<i>Sunflower Girls</i>

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:44.340
<i><i>Sunflower Girls</i></i>

00:06:41.780 --> 00:06:44.330
The <i>SunGirls</i> manga volumes...

00:06:44.330 --> 00:06:47.600
You really do love <i>SunGirls</i>, too, don't you?

00:06:47.950 --> 00:06:50.590
Yeah. The manga, though.

00:06:50.860 --> 00:06:52.340
What about the novels?

00:06:52.340 --> 00:06:53.550
I haven't read them.

00:06:53.550 --> 00:06:56.100
The major plot points are the same,

00:06:56.100 --> 00:06:59.170
but there are a quite a lot of 
differences in the details!

00:06:59.170 --> 00:07:00.350
Ah, yes.

00:07:00.350 --> 00:07:05.110
If you read both versions, the story 
and characters grow even deeper!

00:07:05.110 --> 00:07:06.810
Really?

00:07:06.810 --> 00:07:10.600
When you say that the details are different, 
what kinds of things do you mean?

00:07:10.600 --> 00:07:12.640
During the cultural festival incident...

00:07:12.430 --> 00:07:15.330
Do they really need to 
discuss this right now?

00:07:12.640 --> 00:07:13.300
Yes?

00:07:13.300 --> 00:07:16.110
There was that teacher 
who helped them, right?

00:07:15.740 --> 00:07:18.870
Takumin is really going for it.

00:07:16.110 --> 00:07:17.090
Yes.

00:07:17.090 --> 00:07:19.650
In the novel, that teacher is...

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:20.460
That's surprising.

00:07:20.460 --> 00:07:23.260
Oh! I-I'm sorry. I got carried away.

00:07:23.260 --> 00:07:27.390
And it's also surprising that 
Leadercchi likes shojo manga.

00:07:27.390 --> 00:07:28.540
Is it?

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:31.760
You seem like you'd read manga 
about yankii gangs, meow!

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:35.630
You're unexpectedly quite feminine.

00:07:36.030 --> 00:07:37.810
"Unexpectedly"?

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.480
<i>Sunflower Girls</i>

00:07:38.140 --> 00:07:40.480
<i>Sunflower Girls</i>

00:07:38.840 --> 00:07:40.080
Right.

00:07:40.470 --> 00:07:44.760
Well, shall we leave the discussion 
of <i>SunGirls</i> here, and start working?

00:07:44.760 --> 00:07:47.650
I-I'm sorry. Yes, let's do that.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:48.860
Oh!

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:50.480
What is it this time?

00:07:50.480 --> 00:07:53.860
Club leader! I brought a gift with me!

00:07:53.860 --> 00:07:55.690
Oh, so did I.

00:07:55.690 --> 00:07:56.910
I did, too.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.170
Me, too.

00:07:58.170 --> 00:08:00.860
You really didn't need to.

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:04.400
It isn't much, but...

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:06.380
This isn't much, but...

00:08:06.750 --> 00:08:10.710
This isn't "not much," but that's 
what you're supposed to say, right?

00:08:10.710 --> 00:08:13.350
Not saying that it's something 
delicious when it is,

00:08:13.350 --> 00:08:16.710
is one example of Japanese 
modesty and grace, right?

00:08:17.070 --> 00:08:18.090
I know all about it!

00:08:18.330 --> 00:08:19.840
Thank you!

00:08:19.840 --> 00:08:22.900
But, are all of these snacks?

00:08:22.900 --> 00:08:24.270
Senbei crackers!

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.660
What about yours, Takumin?

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:28.170
Oh! It's a chocolate mille-feuille.

00:08:28.170 --> 00:08:31.980
Pudding gave me mine to 
bring. It's baumkuchen!

00:08:31.980 --> 00:08:35.530
Mine is konpeito candy that 
Haru-neechan recommended I try!

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.200
You've got all-you-can eat snacks!

00:08:40.360 --> 00:08:42.290
Let's all eat them together later.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.620
Hey, Leadercchi...

00:08:43.930 --> 00:08:47.620
Brooches are nice, but I'd like 
to try making this, too, meow!

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:52.550
Sure, but we aren't making things we want, 
we're making things that will sell.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:54.560
Understood, meow!

00:08:54.970 --> 00:08:58.090
I'm going to make tablet stands.

00:08:58.400 --> 00:08:59.680
Sounds good.

00:09:00.010 --> 00:09:01.100
In that case...

00:09:06.280 --> 00:09:09.560
Jobko and Shii can work over here.

00:09:10.160 --> 00:09:12.640
Wow!

00:09:12.640 --> 00:09:15.070
What a wonderful wooden deck!

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.910
That's our club leader for you!

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.290
All right!

00:09:18.290 --> 00:09:21.090
Everyone, let's give it our best!

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:23.080
Do it...

00:09:23.400 --> 00:09:25.560
yourself!

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:48.060
Takumin, you really are 
skilled. That's so delicate!

00:09:49.030 --> 00:09:50.710
What is that?

00:09:51.080 --> 00:09:52.990
UV resin.

00:09:52.990 --> 00:09:55.630
Yoo vee rezen?

00:09:56.400 --> 00:10:00.700
UV resin is a gel that hardens 
when exposed to ultraviolet light.

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:06.660
Well, let's try doing it together.

00:10:07.210 --> 00:10:08.750
Let's see...

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:12.340
First, let's make necklaces 
from the shells we picked up.

00:10:12.340 --> 00:10:13.160
Yes, ma'am!

00:10:13.410 --> 00:10:17.180
Start by using an electric drill to make 
a hole for the cord to pass through.

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.230
Next, use sand mixed with 
clear resin to make a beach.

00:10:23.230 --> 00:10:27.230
Then, put it under the UV light 
to harden the liquid resin.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:32.260
Next, mix clear and blue resin 
together to create a color.

00:10:33.090 --> 00:10:35.810
Using a toothpick makes it easy to mix.

00:10:36.300 --> 00:10:39.560
Pour it in to make an ocean.

00:10:40.050 --> 00:10:42.810
Then, use the UV light to harden it.

00:10:42.810 --> 00:10:46.690
Repeat a few times, and when 
the sea is looking good,

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:48.550
then we'll make some waves.

00:10:49.070 --> 00:10:53.040
Draw a line with white resin 
in a layer of clear resin.

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:55.690
Use a hair dryer to blow on it...

00:10:55.690 --> 00:10:57.630
and a wave pattern will form.

00:10:57.630 --> 00:10:59.720
That's amazing!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:01.090
Once it looks good,

00:11:01.400 --> 00:11:03.710
quickly put it under the UV light to harden.

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.090
Use these for the finishing touch.

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:09.070
Apply a thin layer of resin with a brush.

00:11:09.070 --> 00:11:11.850
Make a collage of things 
like spangles and beads.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:14.730
Once it's been cured under the UV light,

00:11:14.730 --> 00:11:17.270
coat it with clear resin...

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:19.550
and put it under the UV light one last time.

00:11:20.170 --> 00:11:24.290
Once it's cured, pass a leather cord through 
the hole we made at the beginning...

00:11:24.290 --> 00:11:26.040
knot it tightly...

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:27.840
and it's done.

00:11:28.280 --> 00:11:30.900
Oh! It turned out great!

00:11:31.210 --> 00:11:32.840
Or did it?

00:11:32.840 --> 00:11:35.290
There's a lot of bubbles...

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:38.290
Club leader, yours is really pretty.

00:11:38.290 --> 00:11:43.650
As I added resin during the process, I made 
sure to pop the bubbles along the way.

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:46.300
Please tell me stuff like 
that ahead of time!

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.410
I guess it's okay, though!

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:50.320
This adds character, right?

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:53.990
Well, if you're using it 
yourself, that's fine,

00:11:53.990 --> 00:11:57.390
but if you're planning to sell them, 
you should be a little more careful.

00:11:57.750 --> 00:11:59.900
Yes, ma'am! I'll give it a try!

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:06.020
How's it going over there?

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:08.390
Finished cutting, meow.

00:12:08.390 --> 00:12:10.280
Preparations complete.

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:14.210
Then, let's start with the coffee dripper.

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:16.790
We'll put circular holes in these.

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:19.050
Two pieces make up one set,

00:12:19.050 --> 00:12:22.740
so lay down masking tape in a 
crossed pattern to secure them.

00:12:22.740 --> 00:12:27.540
We need to put holes in the 
four corners for the supports.

00:12:27.540 --> 00:12:31.610
If you put tape over them first, 
you'll be less likely to get burrs.

00:12:30.060 --> 00:12:31.810
<b>Like these</b>

00:12:31.610 --> 00:12:34.550
Use a pencil to mark where the 
holes should go, and then...

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:38.990
use a drill driver to start making holes.

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:43.330
Once you've got all the holes for the 
supports in each board finished,

00:12:43.870 --> 00:12:47.080
draw a circle on one board using a compass.

00:12:47.480 --> 00:12:51.090
Use a drill to make rough holes 
along the edge of the circle,

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:52.950
then use a jigsaw to cut it out.

00:12:53.550 --> 00:12:57.100
You want to create a 50 mm diameter 
hole in the center of the board.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:00.070
Use sandpaper on the edges of the hole.

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:02.600
Once all the holes are done,

00:13:02.840 --> 00:13:04.760
use a stain on the wood to add color...

00:13:05.270 --> 00:13:06.910
and improve the finish.

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.550
Next, take the fully threaded 
rod that will form the supports

00:13:10.550 --> 00:13:13.630
and mark it at 170 mm intervals.

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:16.360
Then, use the circular saw to cut it.

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:22.100
Take the fully threaded rods, 
pass them through the four corner holes,

00:13:22.100 --> 00:13:24.110
and use nuts to secure them.

00:13:24.350 --> 00:13:27.190
The nuts just won't go on, meow...

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:32.870
When you cut the rods, you ended up with 
burrs that make it hard for the nut to turn.

00:13:33.160 --> 00:13:35.870
When that happens, you use 
this to take off the burrs.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:40.100
Attach a deburring bit to 
the drill, get it rotating,

00:13:40.100 --> 00:13:42.880
move the end of the rod, 
grinding it against the bit, and...

00:13:45.130 --> 00:13:48.880
Wow! It spins beautifully, meow!

00:13:49.550 --> 00:13:54.620
Finally, slip the upper board over the 
rods and finish them with cap nuts.

00:13:55.700 --> 00:13:57.650
It's done!

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:00.920
It looks very nicely done, 
if I do say so myself, meow!

00:13:59.700 --> 00:14:03.130
Looks like I can leave making 
the coffee drippers to you.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.910
Now, Jobko is...

00:14:06.640 --> 00:14:11.920
Overlap G and H, and drill a 5.5mm hole.

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:18.610
Well...

00:14:18.610 --> 00:14:23.710
Use wood glue to secure the
 three pieces that form the back.

00:14:23.710 --> 00:14:29.670
Add D, E, and G, which you just drilled 
holes into, and secure with screws.

00:14:30.140 --> 00:14:33.940
You should probably temporarily assemble 
the other parts to check the positioning.

00:14:34.670 --> 00:14:37.260
Once I've determined the positions 
of the legs for the stand,

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:38.740
I'll remove them for a minute,

00:14:38.740 --> 00:14:42.180
and before screwing them down, 
I'll use a drill to make pilot holes.

00:14:42.430 --> 00:14:44.690
Then I'll switch to a 
Phillips screwdriver bit...

00:14:44.690 --> 00:14:46.360
and use screws to secure everything.

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:52.870
Parts F and H, which will become the 
legs of the stand, get glued together,

00:14:52.870 --> 00:14:54.450
and then secured with screws.

00:14:54.840 --> 00:15:00.110
Add bolts, wing nuts, and washers, 
then check the movement.

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:02.970
Okay.

00:15:03.180 --> 00:15:06.810
Then, I'll draw a curve on 
the desk with a pencil,

00:15:06.810 --> 00:15:07.970
and use a jigsaw to cut it.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:13.320
The part that will hold the tablet will 
be attached with glue and screws.

00:15:16.190 --> 00:15:20.720
I'll apply glue to the part, 
and affix it to the body.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:24.740
From the back, I'll use screws to secure it.

00:15:24.740 --> 00:15:29.980
Finally, I'll apply stain from the 
side with the curve to add color,

00:15:30.260 --> 00:15:33.250
and the tablet stand is complete!

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:35.330
And that's all there is to it.

00:15:37.170 --> 00:15:40.000
Next, I'll make a different design!

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:47.590
Looks like I can just leave them to it.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.740
And Serufu and Takumin are...

00:15:56.180 --> 00:15:56.980
Ack!

00:15:56.980 --> 00:15:59.210
The resin spilled!

00:15:59.510 --> 00:16:04.440
There's no need to panic. Just wipe it up 
with resin cleaner and it'll be fine.

00:16:04.440 --> 00:16:05.980
That's a relief!

00:16:13.030 --> 00:16:15.290
These are the snacks you gave me earlier.

00:16:15.290 --> 00:16:18.280
Let's eat them together 
and take a little break.

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.430
Yay!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:20.430
Oh!

00:16:23.010 --> 00:16:25.000
So many snacks!

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:28.070
Wow! What a delicious looking sablé!

00:16:28.070 --> 00:16:28.800
Huh?

00:16:28.800 --> 00:16:32.290
Were there cookies in the 
gifts we brought you?

00:16:33.960 --> 00:16:36.960
I... made them.

00:16:36.960 --> 00:16:38.230
What?

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:39.720
Um...

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:42.720
Since everyone was coming today...

00:16:43.220 --> 00:16:45.600
Club leader, you made these yourself?!

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:50.070
Well, from time to time... 
I make them, so...

00:16:50.310 --> 00:16:54.860
It's not just handicraft DIY... you're 
good at making sweets, too!

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:58.610
Leadercchi, you can do 
anything! You're amazing!

00:16:58.610 --> 00:17:01.690
You're just like the 
club leader in <i>SunGirls</i>!

00:17:02.120 --> 00:17:04.710
W-Well... please have some.

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.650
Thank you for the meal!

00:17:07.230 --> 00:17:11.100
Then, I guess I'll have this sablé 
shaped like a hexagonal kite.

00:17:20.110 --> 00:17:21.190
How are they?

00:17:22.380 --> 00:17:24.250
Um...

00:17:24.250 --> 00:17:25.570
Well...

00:17:29.070 --> 00:17:31.970
<i>"They're not yummy because 
they're underbaked."</i>

00:17:32.550 --> 00:17:34.310
<i>I can't tell her that.</i>

00:17:34.620 --> 00:17:36.970
<i>If I tell her honestly...</i>

00:17:37.770 --> 00:17:39.890
<i>She might get angry.</i>

00:17:40.630 --> 00:17:41.510
What's wrong?

00:17:41.510 --> 00:17:44.450
Um, it's disg—

00:17:45.880 --> 00:17:51.470
It's d... Um, d-definitely something I 
want to take my time savoring first.

00:17:52.330 --> 00:17:54.070
Takumin, what do you think?

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:57.120
T-They're delicious!

00:17:57.120 --> 00:18:00.500
If we had an oven set to 180 degrees Celsius,
 and baked them another five minutes,

00:18:00.500 --> 00:18:03.390
they might be even better...?

00:18:03.390 --> 00:18:06.080
Really? I'm so glad!

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:09.130
The manager and director are both nice 
enough to say they're good, too.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:14.830
I thought maybe they were being considerate 
of my feelings when they said that, but...

00:18:15.320 --> 00:18:17.350
Th-They're good.

00:18:17.350 --> 00:18:20.370
They're... baked very well, I think.

00:18:21.290 --> 00:18:24.830
Hearing you two say that they're 
good sets my mind at ease.

00:18:24.830 --> 00:18:26.980
<i>I'm absolutely certain that 
her parents are also...</i>

00:18:26.980 --> 00:18:29.180
<i>being considerate of her feelings.</i>

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:30.990
You can eat as many as you like!

00:18:31.650 --> 00:18:33.700
Then I won't hold back!

00:18:35.540 --> 00:18:38.210
They're so good! So good, meow!

00:18:38.210 --> 00:18:40.270
Huh? Is something wrong?

00:18:40.270 --> 00:18:43.840
Oh! Shii-chan, you can eat all of these!

00:18:43.840 --> 00:18:45.640
Y-Yes!

00:18:45.640 --> 00:18:48.990
We have other sweets, so...

00:18:48.990 --> 00:18:50.480
Are you really sure?!

00:18:56.770 --> 00:18:59.550
What? The cookies are already all gone?

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:02.090
Just how many did you eat?

00:19:04.130 --> 00:19:06.390
Thank you!

00:19:07.140 --> 00:19:11.210
We'll return tomorrow. 
Thank you for having us again.

00:19:11.210 --> 00:19:13.440
If you need to cut large pieces of lumber,

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.610
or if there's anything else I can help with, 
don't hesitate to say, okay?

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:17.620
Will do!

00:19:16.610 --> 00:19:17.620
Yes!

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:19.720
U-Um, director...

00:19:20.020 --> 00:19:23.070
There were some aprons in the workroom.

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:24.920
Are we allowed to have those?

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:26.460
Of course!

00:19:26.810 --> 00:19:28.830
Thank you so much!

00:19:28.830 --> 00:19:32.580
Huh? Takumin, you have an apron, don't you?

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:35.490
Y-Yes, I do...

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:38.250
but there's something I'd like to try.

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:39.530
Huh?

00:19:41.350 --> 00:19:42.400
And so...

00:19:42.760 --> 00:19:47.510
for a while, we'll be working at our 
club leader's place after school.

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:49.870
I might be a little late coming home.

00:19:49.870 --> 00:19:53.620
Really. Well, you seem to be having fun, 
and that's the most important thing.

